    "body": "## Summary\n- scope the pessimistic job lock for live-tracking checkpoint transitions to the authenticated assigned worker\n- return the same not-found response for missing jobs and unauthorized actors, avoiding job-existence disclosure before tracking state is read\n- reject missing persisted actor identity before any repository access\n- add regression coverage proving outsiders cannot read or lock tracking state and the happy path still validates proximity before transition\n\n## Production risk addressed\nThis hardens a P1 privacy/authorization boundary in live tracking. Previously the checkpoint guard locked a job by global ID and only then checked whether the caller was the assigned worker. That allowed unauthorized callers to interact with a real job row before authorization and produced a distinguishable forbidden path. The new query enforces worker ownership in the locked lookup itself.\n\n## Validation\nGitHub Actions required for this repository must pass on the exact PR head before merge. No merge should occur while relevant checks are pending or failing.",
