          },
          "body": "## P1 privacy / authorization hardening\n\nThe live GPS mutation path acquired a global pessimistic lock on a private job before proving that the authenticated caller was the assigned worker. That left the most sensitive tracking write surface inconsistent with participant-scoped reads and the checkpoint hardening merged in #209.\n\n## Final change\n\n- fail closed before repository access when the authenticated principal has no persisted user id;\n- acquire the job through `findAssignedWorkerByIdForUpdate(jobId, workerId)` before any tracking-state read;\n- return the same neutral `404` for a missing job and every non-assigned GPS publisher, including the job owner;\n- only evaluate tracking lifecycle after the assigned-worker-scoped lock succeeds;\n- preserve tracking-row locking, out-of-order protection, GPS quality/speed guards, ETA refresh behavior and terminal cleanup semantics;\n- align runtime smoke with the neutral-not-found mutation privacy boundary.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\nFocused service-level tests prove that an unassigned publisher never reaches the global job lock or tracking state, a principal without a persisted id fails before any repository access, and lifecycle disclosure occurs only after the assigned-worker-scoped lock succeeds.\n\nAn earlier exact-head smoke run correctly exposed the stale owner-`403` expectation. The branch now keeps one coherent fail-closed `404` contract in both implementation and runtime verification. Because the head changed during the correction, only checks for the final current SHA are valid for merge.\n\n## Base / merge gate\n\nThe branch originated from `master` `d5bf27427fbac42d4c9c5abd23d376367b592687` after #209 post-merge CI, CodeQL and Container Security were green.\n\nDo not merge unless every relevant check is green for the exact current PR head, review threads are clear, and `master` is revalidated immediately before merge. Merge with a merge commit only.",
